{{Term/Store|Farosh's Scale|Farosh's Scales|Series, BotW, TotK|plural}} are recurring [[Item]]s in {{TLoZ Series}}.<ref name="BotW Inventory">{{Cite|{{Big|Farosh's Scale}}<br/>This precious scale fell from the golden spirit Farosh. It contains powerful electricity within. You can cook with it, but just eating it seems like a waste.|Inventory|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|{{Big|Farosh's Scale}}<br/>This precious scale is constantly charged with powerful electricity. Attach it to a weapon to greatly increase its attack power. Cooking it is possible but probably wasteful.|Inventory|TotK}}</ref>

==Location and Uses==
==={{BotW|-}}===
Farosh's Scales can be collected from the [[Dragon]] [[Farosh]],<ref name="BotW Inventory" /> who typically flies around [[Lake Hylia]], [[Lake Floria]], and the [[Gerudo Highlands]]. The first time that [[Link]] strikes Farosh, it will yield a Scale regardless of where it was struck, whereas after that he must strike the main portion of its body to receive the Scale. It will subsequently fall somewhere on the land in the form of a light.

[[Cooking]] with Farosh's Scales will always result in [[Dubious Food]]. However, when critters are used in the [[Cooking Pot]], the result will be an [[Elixir]]. At the [[Kochi Dye Shop]], Farosh's Scales can be used as an ingredient to create [[Light Yellow Dye]].

During "[[The Serpent's Jaws]]" [[Shrine Quest]], Link will come upon the [[Spring of Courage]]. When he prays to the [[Goddess Statue]] there, [[Hylia]] will instruct him to offer one of Farosh's Scales to the Spring.<ref>{{Cite|Offer {{Color BotW|Red|Farosh's scale}}, received from the golden spirit, to the {{Color BotW|Blue|Spring of Courage}}. I, Goddess Hylia, will guide you.|Goddess Statue|BotW}}</ref> Doing this will open the way to [[Shae Katha Shrine]].<ref>{{Cite|Just as the Goddess instructed, you threw {{Color BotW|Red|Farosh's scale}} into the Spring of Courage. A shrine appeared as a result!|Adventure Log|BotW}}</ref>

Farosh's Claws are required to upgrade the following pieces of [[Armor]] at a [[Great Fairy Fountain]]:
{{Material Armors|BotW|Farosh's Scale}}

==={{TotK|-}}===
{{Stub|TotK}}

Farosh's Scales are required to upgrade the following pieces of [[Armor]] at a [[Great Fairy Fountain]]:
{{Material Armors|TotK|Farosh's Scale}}

==Trivia==
* In {{BotW}}, Farosh's Scale is the only scale that cannot be collected without hitting its respective [[Dragon]]. Both a [[Naydra's Scale|Naydra's]] and a [[Dinraal's Scale]] can be found in [[Treasure Chest]]s in [[Hyrule Castle (Dungeon)|Hyrule Castle]].

